      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Path analysis can be very useful in quantitative genetics since explicit statements can often be made about causality and sometimes about additivity. Of the following examples, the first two illustrate how path analysis can be used to derive some fundamental relationships concerning phenotypic correlations. The third example considers an empirical problem.",
